{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'rg -n \"''^\" src/gnosis/kernel/replay.py'","aggregated_output":"1:\"\"\"Strict replay + write-ahead intent (Directive 7).\r\n2:\r\n3:Two mechanisms that together make a run reproducible and its side effects\r\n4:decidable, from docs/research/REFERENCE_REPOSITORY_FINDINGS.md §7:\r\n5:\r\n6:**Strict replay (`InteractionStore`).** Every LLM/tool call is recorded\r\n7:under a content hash of its *response-determining* parameters — which the\r\n8:caller declares explicitly in a `CallSpec` rather than the store guessing\r\n9:from an opaque blob. Replay is **occurrence-aware**: the same key called\r\n10:three times replays the first, second and third recorded responses in\r\n11:order, preserving both call order and multiplicity. Replay is **strict by\r\n12:default**: a miss is a `ReplayMiss` abort, never a silent fall-through to\r\n13:a live model (bernstein's `DeterministicStore` rule). Falling through is\r\n14:`ReplayMode.REPLAY_OR_RECORD` — an explicit opt-in, not a default.\r\n15:\r\n16:**Write-ahead intent (`IntentJournal`).** Before a side-effecting tool\r\n17:executes, an `intent.declared` row is persisted carrying the side-effect\r\n18:provenance flags (side_effect, idempotent, has_revert, idempotency_key).\r\n19:The outcome is a second row. Rewind/fork/compensation safety then becomes\r\n20:a *query* over the journal, never a guess: an intent declared with no\r\n21:outcome is precisely the \"did it actually happen?\" case a crash leaves\r\n22:behind, and it is reported as such instead of being assumed either way.\r\n23:\r\n24:The journal is a `RunLedger` (ADR-0004): append-only, hash-chained,\r\n25:tamper-evident, torn-tail tolerant. Keys use `kernel.canonical`, the\r\n26:kernel's single hash contract — no second encoding is introduced here.\r\n27:\"\"\"\r\n28:from __future__ import annotations\r\n29:\r\n30:import json\r\n31:from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator\r\n32:from dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\n33:from enum import Enum\r\n34:from pathlib import Path\r\n35:from types import TracebackType\r\n36:from typing import Any, Self\r\n37:\r\n38:from .canonical import hash_canonical\r\n39:from .file_lock import FileLock, lock_path_for\r\n40:from .ledger import RunLedger\r\n41:\r\n42:INTENT_DECLARED = \"intent.declared\"\r\n43:INTENT_COMPLETED = \"intent.completed\"\r\n44:INTENT_FAILED = \"intent.failed\"\r\n45:\r\n46:\r\n47:class ReplayError(RuntimeError):\r\n48:    pass\r\n49:\r\n50:\r\n51:class ReplayMiss(ReplayError):\r\n52:    \"\"\"Strict replay found no recorded response for this call.\r\n53:\r\n54:    Carries the key and occurrence so a failing replay names exactly what\r\n55:    was missing instead of degrading into a live call.\"\"\"\r\n56:\r\n57:    def __init__(self, spec: CallSpec, occurrence: int, recorded: int):\r\n58:        super().__init__(\r\n59:            f\"replay miss for tool {spec.tool!r} key {spec.key()[:16]}… \"\r\n60:            f\"occurrence {occurrence} (only {recorded} recorded)\"\r\n61:        )\r\n62:        self.spec = spec\r\n63:        self.occurrence = occurrence\r\n64:        self.recorded = recorded\r\n65:\r\n66:\r\n67:class ReplayMode(str, Enum):\r\n68:    RECORD = \"RECORD\"                    # execute live, record the response\r\n69:    REPLAY = \"REPLAY\"                    # strict: a miss aborts\r\n70:    REPLAY_OR_RECORD = \"REPLAY_OR_RECORD\"  # explicit opt-in fall-through\r\n71:\r\n72:\r\n73:@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n74:class CallSpec:\r\n75:    \"\"\"One call, identified by its response-determining parameters.\r\n76:\r\n77:    ``params`` must contain everything that can change the response\r\n78:    (model, provider, temperature, max_tokens, effort, prompt, tool\r\n79:    arguments…) and nothing that cannot (timestamps, durations, request\r\n80:    ids). Anything non-determining belongs in ``metadata``, which is\r\n81:    recorded but never keyed — folding a timestamp into the key would\r\n82:    make every replay a miss.\"\"\"\r\n83:\r\n84:    tool: str\r\n85:    params: dict[str, Any]\r\n86:    metadata: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\r\n87:\r\n88:    def key(self) -> str:\r\n89:        return hash_canonical({\"tool\": self.tool, \"params\": self.params})\r\n90:\r\n91:\r\n92:@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n93:class InteractionRecord:\r\n94:    key: str\r\n95:    tool: str\r\n96:    occurrence: int\r\n97:    params: dict[str, Any]\r\n98:    response: Any\r\n99:    metadata: dict[str, Any] = field(default_factory=dict)\r\n100:\r\n101:    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n102:        return {\r\n103:            \"key\": self.key, \"tool\": self.tool, \"occurrence\": self.occurrence,\r\n104:            \"params\": self.params, \"response\": self.response, \"metadata\": self.metadata,\r\n105:        }\r\n106:\r\n107:    @classmethod\r\n108:    def from_dict(cls, data: dict[str, Any]) -> InteractionRecord:\r\n109:        return cls(\r\n110:            key=data[\"key\"], tool=data[\"tool\"], occurrence=data[\"occurrence\"],\r\n111:            params=data[\"params\"], response=data[\"response\"],\r\n112:            metadata=data.get(\"metadata\", {}),\r\n113:        )\r\n114:\r\n115:\r\n116:class InteractionStore:\r\n117:    \"\"\"Occurrence-aware, content-addressed cassette of recorded calls.\r\n118:\r\n119:    One append-only JSONL file. Recording appends; replaying consumes\r\n120:    per-key FIFO cursors held in memory for the life of this instance, so\r\n121:    a fresh instance replays a run from the beginning — replay is a\r\n122:    property of the run, not of the process.\r\n123:    \"\"\"\r\n124:\r\n125:    def __init__(self, path: Path, mode: ReplayMode = ReplayMode.RECORD,\r\n126:                 lock_timeout_s: float = 30.0):\r\n127:        self.path = path\r\n128:        self.mode = mode\r\n129:        self._lock_timeout_s = lock_timeout_s\r\n130:        self.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n131:        self._by_key: dict[str, list[InteractionRecord]] = {}\r\n132:        self._cursor: dict[str, int] = {}\r\n133:        self._load()\r\n134:\r\n135:    # -- recording / replaying ------------------------------------------\r\n136:\r\n137:    def call(self, spec: CallSpec, live_fn: Callable[[], Any]) -> Any:\r\n138:        \"\"\"Return this call's response, from the cassette or live, per mode.\r\n139:\r\n140:        ``live_fn`` is invoked only when the mode allows a live call; in\r\n141:        strict REPLAY it is never invoked, so a replayed run cannot reach\r\n142:        the network even if a key is missing.\r\n143:        \"\"\"\r\n144:        occurrence = self._cursor.get(spec.key(), 0)\r\n145:        if self.mode in (ReplayMode.REPLAY, ReplayMode.REPLAY_OR_RECORD):\r\n146:            recorded = self._by_key.get(spec.key(), [])\r\n147:            if occurrence < len(recorded):\r\n148:                self._cursor[spec.key()] = occurrence + 1\r\n149:                return recorded[occurrence].response\r\n150:            if self.mode is ReplayMode.REPLAY:\r\n151:                raise ReplayMiss(spec, occurrence, len(recorded))\r\n152:        response = live_fn()\r\n153:        # Return the ROUND-TRIPPED value, not the live object: a recording\r\n154:        # run and a replaying run must observe byte-identical responses, or\r\n155:        # \"deterministic replay\" is a lie the first time a tuple comes back\r\n156:        # as a list. Verified: without this, RECORD saw ('a','b') where\r\n157:        # REPLAY saw ['a','b'].\r\n158:        recorded = self._append(spec, occurrence, response)\r\n159:        self._cursor[spec.key()] = occurrence + 1\r\n160:        return recorded.response\r\n161:\r\n162:    def replayed_count(self, spec: CallSpec) -> int:\r\n163:        return self._cursor.get(spec.key(), 0)\r\n164:\r\n165:    def records(self) -> list[InteractionRecord]:\r\n166:        out: list[InteractionRecord] = []\r\n167:        for records in self._by_key.values():\r\n168:            out.extend(records)\r\n169:        return sorted(out, key=lambda r: (r.key, r.occurrence))\r\n170:\r\n171:    def unused(self) -> list[InteractionRecord]:\r\n172:        \"\"\"Recorded interactions this replay never consumed — the signal\r\n173:        that a golden fixture and the current code have diverged.\"\"\"\r\n174:        return [\r\n175:            record\r\n176:            for key, records in self._by_key.items()\r\n177:            for record in records[self._cursor.get(key, 0):]\r\n178:        ]\r\n179:\r\n180:    # -- internals -------------------------------------------------------\r\n181:\r\n182:    def _append(self, spec: CallSpec, occurrence: int, response: Any) -> InteractionRecord:\r\n183:        record = InteractionRecord(\r\n184:            key=spec.key(), tool=spec.tool, occurrence=occurrence,\r\n185:            params=spec.params, response=response, metadata=spec.metadata,\r\n186:        )\r\n187:        try:\r\n188:            line = json.dumps(record.to_dict(), sort_keys=True, allow_nan=False)\r\n189:        except (TypeError, ValueError) as exc:\r\n190:            # A response that cannot be recorded cannot be replayed, and a\r\n191:            # cassette missing one call silently mis-aligns every later\r\n192:            # occurrence. Fail loudly and name the tool instead.\r\n193:            raise ReplayError(\r\n194:                f\"response from tool {spec.tool!r} is not JSON-representable \"\r\n195:                f\"and therefore not replayable: {exc}\"\r\n196:            ) from exc\r\n197:        # Re-read what was actually serialized: this is the value the store\r\n198:        # returns and the value a later replay will produce.\r\n199:        record = InteractionRecord.from_dict(json.loads(line))\r\n200:        with (\r\n201:            FileLock(lock_path_for(self.path), timeout_s=self._lock_timeout_s),\r\n202:            self.path.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh,\r\n203:        ):\r\n204:            fh.write(line + \"\\n\")\r\n205:        self._by_key.setdefault(record.key, []).append(record)\r\n206:        return record\r\n207:\r\n208:    def _load(self) -> None:\r\n209:        if not self.path.exists():\r\n210:            return\r\n211:        for index, line in enumerate(self.path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()):\r\n212:            line = line.strip()\r\n213:            if not line:\r\n214:                continue\r\n215:            try:\r\n216:                record = InteractionRecord.from_dict(json.loads(line))\r\n217:            except (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as exc:\r\n218:                raise ReplayError(\r\n219:                    f\"corrupt cassette line {index + 1} in {self.path}: {exc}\"\r\n220:                ) from exc\r\n221:            self._by_key.setdefault(record.key, []).append(record)\r\n222:        for records in self._by_key.values():\r\n223:            records.sort(key=lambda r: r.occurrence)\r\n224:\r\n225:\r\n226:# -- write-ahead intent ---------------------------------------------------\r\n227:\r\n228:\r\n229:class IntentStatus(str, Enum):\r\n230:    DECLARED = \"DECLARED\"    # persisted, outcome unknown (crash window)\r\n231:    COMPLETED = \"COMPLETED\"\r\n232:    FAILED = \"FAILED\"\r\n233:\r\n234:\r\n235:@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n236:class SideEffect:\r\n237:    \"\"\"Provenance of what a tool call is about to do.\r\n238:\r\n239:    ``idempotent``: re-running it is safe. ``has_revert``: a compensating\r\n240:    action exists. ``idempotency_key``: the token a remote system uses to\r\n241:    deduplicate a retry.\"\"\"\r\n242:\r\n243:    side_effect: bool\r\n244:    idempotent: bool = False\r\n245:    has_revert: bool = False\r\n246:    idempotency_key: str | None = None\r\n247:\r\n248:    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n249:        return {\r\n250:            \"side_effect\": self.side_effect, \"idempotent\": self.idempotent,\r\n251:            \"has_revert\": self.has_revert, \"idempotency_key\": self.idempotency_key,\r\n252:        }\r\n253:\r\n254:    @classmethod\r\n255:    def from_dict(cls, data: dict[str, Any]) -> SideEffect:\r\n256:        return cls(\r\n257:            side_effect=data[\"side_effect\"], idempotent=data.get(\"idempotent\", False),\r\n258:            has_revert=data.get(\"has_revert\", False),\r\n259:            idempotency_key=data.get(\"idempotency_key\"),\r\n260:        )\r\n261:\r\n262:\r\n263:@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n264:class IntentRecord:\r\n265:    intent_id: str\r\n266:    tool: str\r\n267:    status: IntentStatus\r\n268:    effect: SideEffect\r\n269:    params: dict[str, Any]\r\n270:    outcome: dict[str, Any] | None = None\r\n271:\r\n272:    @property\r\n273:    def unresolved(self) -> bool:\r\n274:        \"\"\"Declared with no outcome: the crash window where whether the\r\n275:        side effect landed is unknown.\"\"\"\r\n276:        return self.status is IntentStatus.DECLARED\r\n277:\r\n278:    @property\r\n279:    def blocks_rewind(self) -> bool:\r\n280:        \"\"\"A side effect that can be neither safely repeated nor undone —\r\n281:        rewinding past it is unsafe, and the journal says so rather than\r\n282:        the caller guessing.\"\"\"\r\n283:        return self.effect.side_effect and not self.effect.idempotent and not self.effect.has_revert\r\n284:\r\n285:\r\n286:class IntentJournal:\r\n287:    \"\"\"Write-ahead journal of side-effecting intents, on a hash-chained\r\n288:    RunLedger (ADR-0004): append-only and tamper-evident.\r\n289:\r\n290:    Usage::\r\n291:\r\n292:        with journal.intent(\"git.push\", effect, params) as handle:\r\n293:            do_the_thing()\r\n294:            handle.complete({\"pushed\": True})\r\n295:\r\n296:    The declaration is durable BEFORE the body runs; an exception marks\r\n297:    the intent failed and propagates; a crash leaves it DECLARED, which\r\n298:    ``unresolved()`` reports as an open question rather than assuming\r\n299:    either outcome.\r\n300:    \"\"\"\r\n301:\r\n302:    def __init__(self, ledger: RunLedger, run_id: str):\r\n303:        self.ledger = ledger\r\n304:        self.run_id = run_id\r\n305:        self._counter = 0\r\n306:\r\n307:    def intent(self, tool: str, effect: SideEffect,\r\n308:               params: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> _IntentHandle:\r\n309:        self._counter += 1\r\n310:        intent_id = f\"INTENT-{self._counter:04d}-{hash_canonical({'tool': tool, 'n': self._counter})[:8]}\"\r\n311:        payload = {\r\n312:            \"intent_id\": intent_id, \"tool\": tool, \"effect\": effect.to_dict(),\r\n313:            \"params\": params or {},\r\n314:        }\r\n315:        # Durable BEFORE the side effect: this ordering is the whole point.\r\n316:        self.ledger.append(self.run_id, INTENT_DECLARED, payload)\r\n317:        return _IntentHandle(self, intent_id, tool, effect, params or {})\r\n318:\r\n319:    def _record_outcome(self, intent_id: str, event_type: str,\r\n320:                        outcome: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\r\n321:        self.ledger.append(self.run_id, event_type,\r\n322:                           {\"intent_id\": intent_id, \"outcome\": outcome})\r\n323:\r\n324:    # -- queries (rewind safety is answered here, never guessed) ---------\r\n325:\r\n326:    def records(self) -> list[IntentRecord]:\r\n327:        declared: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\r\n328:        status: dict[str, IntentStatus] = {}\r\n329:        outcomes: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\r\n330:        order: list[str] = []\r\n331:        for event in self.ledger.read_all():\r\n332:            if event.event_type == INTENT_DECLARED:\r\n333:                intent_id = event.data[\"intent_id\"]\r\n334:                declared[intent_id] = event.data\r\n335:                status[intent_id] = IntentStatus.DECLARED\r\n336:                order.append(intent_id)\r\n337:            elif event.event_type in (INTENT_COMPLETED, INTENT_FAILED):\r\n338:                intent_id = event.data[\"intent_id\"]\r\n339:                if intent_id in declared:\r\n340:                    status[intent_id] = (\r\n341:                        IntentStatus.COMPLETED if event.event_type == INTENT_COMPLETED\r\n342:                        else IntentStatus.FAILED\r\n343:                    )\r\n344:                    outcomes[intent_id] = event.data.get(\"outcome\", {})\r\n345:        return [\r\n346:            IntentRecord(\r\n347:                intent_id=intent_id, tool=declared[intent_id][\"tool\"],\r\n348:                status=status[intent_id],\r\n349:                effect=SideEffect.from_dict(declared[intent_id][\"effect\"]),\r\n350:                params=declared[intent_id].get(\"params\", {}),\r\n351:                outcome=outcomes.get(intent_id),\r\n352:            )\r\n353:            for intent_id in order\r\n354:        ]\r\n355:\r\n356:    def unresolved(self) -> list[IntentRecord]:\r\n357:        \"\"\"Intents declared with no recorded outcome — after a crash these\r\n358:        are exactly the calls whose side effect may or may not have\r\n359:        landed, and they must be resolved by inspection, not assumption.\"\"\"\r\n360:        return [r for r in self.records() if r.unresolved]\r\n361:\r\n362:    def rewind_blockers(self) -> list[IntentRecord]:\r\n363:        \"\"\"Side effects that neither repeat safely nor revert, plus every\r\n364:        unresolved intent (an unknown outcome cannot be declared safe).\"\"\"\r\n365:        return [r for r in self.records() if r.blocks_rewind or r.unresolved]\r\n366:\r\n367:    def can_rewind(self) -> bool:\r\n368:        return not self.rewind_blockers()\r\n369:\r\n370:\r\n371:class _IntentHandle:\r\n372:    \"\"\"Context manager returned by ``IntentJournal.intent``.\"\"\"\r\n373:\r\n374:    def __init__(self, journal: IntentJournal, intent_id: str, tool: str,\r\n375:                 effect: SideEffect, params: dict[str, Any]):\r\n376:        self.journal = journal\r\n377:        self.intent_id = intent_id\r\n378:        self.tool = tool\r\n379:        self.effect = effect\r\n380:        self.params = params\r\n381:        self._resolved = False\r\n382:\r\n383:    def complete(self, outcome: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> None:\r\n384:        if self._resolved:\r\n385:            raise ReplayError(f\"intent {self.intent_id} already resolved\")\r\n386:        self.journal._record_outcome(self.intent_id, INTENT_COMPLETED, outcome or {})\r\n387:        self._resolved = True\r\n388:\r\n389:    def fail(self, outcome: dict[str, Any] | None = None) -> None:\r\n390:        if self._resolved:\r\n391:            raise ReplayError(f\"intent {self.intent_id} already resolved\")\r\n392:        self.journal._record_outcome(self.intent_id, INTENT_FAILED, outcome or {})\r\n393:        self._resolved = True\r\n394:\r\n395:    def __enter__(self) -> Self:\r\n396:        return self\r\n397:\r\n398:    def __exit__(\r\n399:        self,\r\n400:        exc_type: type[BaseException] | None,\r\n401:        exc: BaseException | None,\r\n402:        tb: TracebackType | None,\r\n403:    ) -> None:\r\n404:        if self._resolved:\r\n405:            return\r\n406:        if exc_type is not None:\r\n407:            # The body raised: record the failure, then let it propagate.\r\n408:            # An exception is not proof the side effect did NOT land, but\r\n409:            # it IS a recorded outcome, which unresolved() must not claim.\r\n410:            self.journal._record_outcome(\r\n411:                self.intent_id, INTENT_FAILED, {\"error\": repr(exc)},\r\n412:            )\r\n413:            self._resolved = True\r\n414:            return\r\n415:        # Body finished without saying what happened. Leaving the intent\r\n416:        # DECLARED (rather than inventing a completion) is deliberate: an\r\n417:        # unclaimed outcome is exactly the state unresolved() exists to\r\n418:        # report.\r\n419:\r\n420:\r\n421:def golden_fixture(store: InteractionStore) -> Iterator[dict[str, Any]]:\r\n422:    \"\"\"Recorded interactions as fixture rows — a golden run becomes a\r\n423:    regression fixture (catacomb's pattern) without a second format.\"\"\"\r\n424:    for record in store.records():\r\n425:        yield record.to_dict()\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
