{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Resumed or concurrent journals reuse intent IDs and can erase an unresolved dangerous intent\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/replay.py\",\"line\":310,\"severity\":\"critical\",\"claim\":\"intent_id depends only on a per-instance counter and tool name; records() keys declarations/outcomes solely by that ID and does not scope events by run_id.\",\"scenario\":\"A crashed journal declares INTENT-0001 for an irreversible side effect. A resumed/new journal on the same ledger declares the same tool as its first intent with side_effect=False and completes it. The second declaration overwrites the first in records(), so both entries appear completed and safe; can_rewind() can return true although the original side effect has an unknown outcome.\"},{\"title\":\"Cassette occurrence allocation is not serialized across store instances or threads\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/replay.py\",\"line\":144,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The occurrence is derived from an instance-local cursor before live execution and before acquiring the file lock.\",\"scenario\":\"Two InteractionStore instances (or overlapping calls) record the same CallSpec. Both select occurrence 0, then append under the lock. If the later-started call finishes first, its response becomes the first replayed response. Replay remains strict but no longer preserves the original per-key call order/multiplicity contract.\"},{\"title\":\"Rewind-safety queries consume an unverified ledger\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/replay.py\",\"line\":331,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"records() calls read_all() rather than verify_chain(), so can_rewind() and rewind_blockers() trust tampered chain contents.\",\"scenario\":\"After an irreversible intent is recorded, modifying its effect flags or outcome without recomputing event hashes makes records() report the altered data and can permit rewind. The ledger detects this only if a separate caller explicitly invokes verify_chain().\"},{\"title\":\"A live call returning bytes or NaN is executed but never recorded\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/replay.py\",\"line\":152,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"live_fn runs before response serialization; bytes/NaN then cause _append() to raise, leaving no cassette row for a call that already occurred.\",\"scenario\":\"A side-effecting tool returns bytes after successfully acting. call() raises ReplayError, but a caller that handles it and continues records the next same-key call at occurrence 0. A later replay either replays that later response for the first call or misses, violating the requirement to record every tool call and preserve occurrence alignment.\"}],\"overall\":\"FAIL: the unit has real safety and determinism defects in intent identity/folding, concurrent cassette recording, verified safety queries, and unsupported live response handling.\"}"}}
